;; si, Scheme's evaluator (go/arbace/scm), reached from Arbace (doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, SC61 (a), SC240; "As built: the
;; embedding's gaps"): one static native, whose Go side is go/arbace/scminterp's SchemeInterp_RunProgram_String_String1_String_String1_I__I_native
;; (j2g translates a native of this class into a call of scminterp's, as arbace.lang.CInterp's are cinterp's and
;; arbace.lang.GoInterp's goi's, GOI-SPEC §4.11). arbace.scheme.interp calls it with psyntax's expanded system read from the
;; program's embedded resource scheme/psyntax/psyntax.pp.ss (arbace.scheme.resource).

(in-ns 'arbace.lang)

(defclass ^:public ^:final SchemeInterp
  (constructor ^:private [this])
  ;; runs the Scheme program in the file named file on si, psyntax booted from pp (psyntax.pp as Scheme text) with the library
  ;; path libs, (command-line) file then args, on the process's standard streams, as test/scheme/si-driver runs one: the
  ;; program's exit status, 255 for an uncaught raise (reported on the standard error as Chez reports it), 2 when the file
  ;; cannot be read. flags: 1 the driver's --case (the file's leading libraries installed first, SI-RUN and SI-RAISE on the
  ;; standard error), 2 --r7rs, 4 --core (the file's core forms run without psyntax; pp unused)
  (method ^:public ^:static ^:native runProgram ^int [^String pp ^String/1 libs ^String file ^String/1 args ^int flags]))
